+### Diagnosing configuration
+
+`python -m payhook doctor` prints every setting with its effective value and where it came from (`env`, `.env` or `default`), plus the `.env` path it looked at. Secrets (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are shown only as "set" and their length, never the value, so the output is safe to paste into a support ticket. The command always exits 0.
